    "title": "<p>Syndromic familial non-medullary thyroid carcinoma</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "José Manuel Cameselle-Teijeiro",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 136.141px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Syndrome</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 77.3281px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"11%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Gene (locus), inheritance</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 72.7812px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"11%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Gene MIM number</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.984px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"21%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Thyroid lesions [incidence]</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 273.891px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Other lesions</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 136.141px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PTEN</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> hamartoma tumour syndrome</span></strong> <span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{20301661; 26522472; 21956414}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 77.3281px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"11%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PTEN</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> (10q23.31), AD</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 72.7812px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"11%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">158350</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.984px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"21%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PTC (classic and follicular variant) [60%]; FTC [14&ndash;45%]; HCC [~1%]; ATC [&lt;&nbsp;1%]; FTA (HCA, lipoadenoma, and microadenomas) [25%]; TFND [43&ndash;75%]; C-cell hyperplasia; lymphocytic thyroiditis [55%]</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 273.891px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Pathognomonic criteria:</span></em><sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">a</span></sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Adult Lhermitte&ndash;Duclos disease (cerebellar tumours), facial trichilemmomas, acral keratosis, papillomatous papules, autism spectrum disorder</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Major criteria:</span></em><sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">a</span></sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Breast cancer, macrocephaly, endometrial carcinoma, multiple palmoplantar keratosis, multifocal cutaneous facial papules, macular pigmentation of the glans penis, multiple gastrointestinal hamartomas or ganglioneuromas</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Minor criteria:</span></em><sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">a</span></sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Single gastrointestinal hamartoma or ganglioneuroma, fibrocystic breast disease, lipomas, fibromas, genitourinary tumours (particularly renal cell carcinoma), genitourinary malformations, uterine fibroids, intellectual disability (IQ &le;&nbsp;75)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 136.141px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Familial adenomatous polyposis</span></strong> <span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{29785019; 11232035; 32024448}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 77.3281px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"11%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">APC</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> (5q22.2), AD</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 72.7812px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"11%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">611731</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.984px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"21%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Cribriform-morular thyroid carcinoma [16%]</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 273.891px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Adenomatous polyps of the large bowel, colorectal adenocarcinoma, duodenal adenomas and carcinomas, GAPPS, desmoid tumours, hepatobiliary tree tumours, hepatoblastoma, adrenocortical adenomas and carcinomas, brain tumours, CHRPE</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 136.141px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">DICER1</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> syndrome</span></strong> <span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{30715996; 28323992; 24761742; 29474644}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 77.3281px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"11%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">DICER1</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> (14q32.13), AD</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 72.7812px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"11%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">606241</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.984px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"21%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">TC (PTC, FTC, PDTC)<sup>b</sup>; FTA; TFND</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 273.891px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Macrocephaly, PPB, peritoneal PPB, pulmonary cysts and/or pneumothorax in a newborn or young child, ovarian tumours (Sertoli&ndash;Leydig cell tumour, gynandroblastoma, undifferentiated sarcomas, embryonal rhabdomyosarcoma), ciliary body medulloepithelioma, pituitary blastoma, CNS sarcoma, CNS embryonal tumours, pineoblastoma, nasal chondromesenchymal hamartoma, multicystic hepatic lesions, cystic nephroma, presacral teratoid neoplasm</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 136.141px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Carney complex</span></strong> <span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{19293268; 33444222; 9215269; 20301463}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 77.3281px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"11%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PRKAR1A</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> (17q24.2), AD</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 72.7812px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"11%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">188830</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.984px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"21%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">TC (FTC, PTC) [15%]; TFND (follicular adenomatosis); FTA</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 273.891px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Major criteria:</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Spotty skin pigmentation (lips, conjunctiva and inner or outer canthi, vaginal and penile mucosa), myxoma (cutaneous, mucosal, cardiac, breast), growth hormone&ndash;producing pituitary adenoma, primary pigmented nodular adrenocortical disease, blue naevus and pigmented epithelioid melanocytoma (multiple), breast ductal adenoma (multiple), osteochondromyxoma, psammomatous melanotic schwannoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 136.141px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Werner syndrome</span></strong> <span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{10189141; 8722214; 20301687}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 77.3281px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"11%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">WRN</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> (8p12), AR</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 72.7812px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"11%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">604611</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 151.984px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"21%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">TC (FTC, PTC, ATC) [18%]</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 273.891px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"37%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Bilateral ocular cataracts, premature greying and/or thinning of scalp hair, short stature, chronic ulcers around the ankles, meningioma, melanoma, soft tissue sarcomas, osteosarcomas, leukaemia and preleukaemic disorders, atherosclerotic disease, diabetes mellitus, hypogonadism</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">AD, autosomal dominant; AR, autosomal recessive; ATC, anaplastic thyroid carcinoma; CHRPE, congenital hypertrophy of the retinal pigment epithelium; FTA, follicular thyroid adenoma; FTC, follicular thyroid carcinoma; GAPPS, gastric adenocarcinoma and proximal polyposis of the stomach; HCA, H&uuml;rthle cell adenoma; HCC, H&uuml;rthle cell carcinoma; PDTC, poorly differentiated thyroid carcinoma; PPB, pleuropulmonary blastoma; PTC, papillary thyroid carcinoma; TC, thyroid carcinoma; TFND, thyroid follicular nodular disease.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">a</span></sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\">According</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> to the International Cowden Consortium (ICC) operational diagnostic criteria, non-medullary thyroid cancer is a major criterion, and FTA and TFND are minor criteria </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{21194675}</span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">. <sup>b</sup>Individuals with <em>DICER1</em> syndrome had a 16-fold increased risk of thyroid cancer </span><span class=\"Ref-PMID\" style=\"color: #984806; background: #ccc0d9;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">{28323992}</span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">.</span></p>",
